Parent: 1478

## Context
The 2026-11-09 claims rollout moved the erg pin three times in a day (9ab13c9 -> dafb1d48 ->
6a104262 -> 513cd3c4) and showed three silent drifts: a host PATH `erg` left on an old build
(padme ~/.local/bin/erg, 2c490b7), repos left on a superseded pin until their next refresh (ten
on dafb1d48), and clones whose core.hooksPath pointed at a dead directory, so no hook ever ran
(padme aedist-technical-report, chemin-de-voix, fuzzy-corpus; doudou cadens, aedist, Fuzzy
Corpus). Author decision (2026-11-09): lair must not update erg itself (it would take git-erg's
main, "too fresh"); detect drift and repair only what is local and safe.

## Design (author ruling: git-erg is optional, the harness is tolerant)
- One pin, recorded once in the harness: sha256 plus git-erg revision. Moving it is an author
  decision landed by harness PR; later a signed release tag replaces the hash.
- yawn (read-only) reports, per project and host: `tickets/erg` sha256 vs the pin; PATH `erg`
  vs the pin; `tickets/.claims/` present; core.hooksPath dead or alive.
- molt repairs the local, safe part: unset a dead core.hooksPath, re-run `tickets/erg install
  --hooks`. A binary behind the pin: one ticket in that project (or the rollout recipe when the
  author moved the pin), never an import of an unpinned binary.
- lair: no change; it surfaces molt's findings.
- Tolerance: a project without `tickets/erg`, a store without `.claims/`, a host without a PATH
  `erg`, or a harness checkout with no pin file is not a finding: report "n/a" (or nothing) and
  continue. Only a present erg that differs from the pin, or a hook path that names a missing
  directory, counts. No check may fail a gate or block a merge; Codex and Pi sessions read the
  same report.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] the pin lives in one harness file; tracker 1478 and the rollout recipe cite it
- [ ] yawn reports the four conditions above; tests cover pinned, drifted, absent-erg (n/a),
      no-claims (n/a) and dead-hooksPath cases
- [ ] molt unsets a dead hooksPath and re-installs hooks; files a ticket for a binary behind the
      pin; never imports a binary
- [ ] no new gate failure: a project or host without erg passes every check unchanged
